  "anchors": {
    "What if one CPU could run many apps safely?": 0.0,
    "Why do we virtualize a CPU?": 3.18,
    "Efficiency means the system can handle more work without adding hardware, using time slices so each program gets a turn. Security means each program runs in its own sandbox, so a mistake in one cannot affect the others.": 10.18,
    "Virtualization lets one CPU be efficient and secure.": 40.52,
    "Try drawing your own flow diagram of how a virtual CPU schedules tasks.": 44.2
